# Who reviews what.
#
# Ownership does not mean only the owner may change a directory. It means
# someone is accountable for that module staying coherent, reviews are routed
# without anyone having to guess, and an architectural change cannot happen
# invisibly. Every module in ARCHITECTURE.md appears here; a directory with no
# owner is a directory that decays.
#
# The team names below are placeholders for a single-maintainer repository.
# Replace them with real GitHub teams before enabling required review.

# Fallback: anything not claimed below.
*                               @platform

# The shared kernel. Everything imports it, so changes here reach everywhere
# and are reviewed by the people who own the consequences.
/packages/core/                 @platform

# Infrastructure primitives.
/packages/observability/        @platform
/packages/security/             @platform @identity
/packages/storage/              @platform

# Protocol adapters.
/packages/oauth/                @identity
/packages/mcp-client/           @protocol
/packages/mcp-server/           @protocol

# The business capability.
/packages/federation/           @federation

# Composition and deployables.
/packages/gateway/              @platform
/apps/                          @platform

# Tests.
/conformance/                   @platform
/conformance/tests/security.test.ts     @platform @identity

# The architecture itself. A change to the policy changes what CI permits, so
# it is reviewed alongside the decision record that justifies it.
/ARCHITECTURE.md                @platform
/CONTRIBUTING.md                @platform
/CODEOWNERS                     @platform
/tooling/architecture/          @platform
/docs/architecture/             @platform
/docs/decisions/                @platform
/.github/workflows/             @platform
